rm that's a painfully stupid series. To give you an example, they once made a reportage on Assassin's Creed as if it was realistic and plausible, and even got their facts wrong. The high point of the episode was when the presenter &quot;revived&quot; a past life under hypnosis and it happened to be, <i>what a coincidence</i>, a soldier in the Italian Renaissance who randomly spotted eagles on the battlefield*. Yeah. I figured out exactly what sort of historians we're talking about as soon as I read they were involved with that transmission.<br /> <br /> It does not help that most my friends watch it (it's on prime time on one of the most popular channels) and talk about it as it's gospel and all I want to do is to repeatedly smack them in the head with a heavy chandelier while shouting a &quot;WRONG!&quot; that would make Kevin Spacey proud.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Those who played AC as I did, especially the Ezio's saga, will understand why this so cringeworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-19-2014, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:00:29-07:00","id":174244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=172959#post172959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, sweet! I love mining half-baked conspiracy theories for campaign ideas!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this how people come up with ideas for games or campaign ideas? Pretty lazy there I guess...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=173070#post173070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THIS IS EXACTLY WHAT THE ORDO WANTS YOU TO THINK.<br /> <br /> Alternatively:<br /> <br /> THIS IS EXACTLY WHAT THE CAMARILLA WANTS YOU TO THINK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though I know this is a joke but I would like to point out that this is a example of how conspiracy theories become a mental trap, if anyone tries to debunk a conspiracy/fringe theory/pseudoscience and then it becomes part of the conspiracy which this is called <a href=\"http://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Shill_gambit\" target=\"_blank\">Shill Gambit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-19-2014, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:42:17-07:00","id":174272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=173862#post173862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, Mistero. As an Italian with a childhood passion for occult, folklore, myths and unexplained weirdness who gave that program a shot only to be sorely disappointed, I can confirm that's a painfully stupid series. To give you an example, they once made a reportage on Assassin's Creed as if it was realistic and plausible, and even got their facts wrong. The high point of the episode was when the presenter &quot;revived&quot; a past life under hypnosis and it happened to be, <i>what a coincidence</i>, a soldier in the Italian Renaissance who randomly spotted eagles on the battlefield*. Yeah. I figured out exactly what sort of historians we're talking about as soon as I read they were involved with that transmission.<br /> <br /> It does not help that most my friends watch it (it's on prime time on one of the most popular channels) and talk about it as it's gospel and all I want to do is to repeatedly smack them in the head with a heavy chandelier while shouting a &quot;WRONG!&quot; that would make Kevin Spacey proud.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Those who played AC as I did, especially the Ezio's saga, will understand why this so cringeworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://forum.quattroruote.it/upload/2013/10/30/d0ec7096fe881d7bd7939400dff8acb4_7745.jpg__thumb\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:05:35-07:00","id":174289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174244#post174244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is this how people come up with ideas for games or campaign ideas? Pretty lazy there I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that was rude. I look to all sorts of sources for inspiration, conspiracy theories just happen to be one of the most entertaining sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:37:50-07:00","id":174376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174244#post174244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even though I know this is a joke but I would like to point out that this is a example of how conspiracy theories become a mental trap, if anyone tries to debunk a conspiracy/fringe theory/pseudoscience and then it becomes part of the conspiracy which this is called <a href=\"http://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Shill_gambit\" target=\"_blank\">Shill Gambit</a></div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah. That kinda<i> was</i> the joke...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T12:55:37-07:00","id":174479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174289#post174289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well that was rude. I look to all sorts of sources for inspiration, conspiracy theories just happen to be one of the most entertaining sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon my rudeness but conspiracy theories aren't really the best sources especially how impractical they actually are because well even though there are small scale conspiracies however (like Watergate, Iran Contra, etc) but larger the conspiracy is the more implausible it becomes.<br /> <br /> Especially taking anything fringe as sources undermines the original context that they're taken off from which is why I despise any medium that uses &quot;Ancient Astronauts&quot; or &quot;Lost (often more than likely White) Civilizations&quot; like Assassin's Creed and such because they are insult to any educated person's intelligence not to mention the Colonialist roots that it stems from, just like modern conspiracy theories are stemmed from antisemitism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-19-2014, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:08:46-07:00","id":174492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174479#post174479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pardon my rudeness but conspiracy theories aren't really the best sources especially how impractical they actually are because well even though there are small scale conspiracies however (like Watergate, Iran Contra, etc) but larger the conspiracy is the more implausible it becomes. Especially taking anything fringe as sources undermines the original context that they're taken off from which is why I despise any medium that uses Ancient Astronauts or &amp;quot;Lost (often more than likely White) Civilizations&amp;quot; like Assassin's Creed and such because they are insult to any educated person's intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's fiction. In a game where werewolves and vampires are running around, I'm not terribly concerned with plausibility. Plus, it's not like I'm directly reproducing entire elaborate theories. That's why it's called inspiration and not plagiarism, I just look to them for cool ideas for &quot;what if&quot; scenarios that can spawn original chronicle ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:26:52-07:00","id":174504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174492#post174492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's fiction. In a game where werewolves and vampires are running around, I'm not terribly concerned with plausibility. Plus, it's not like I'm directly reproducing entire elaborate theories. That's why it's called inspiration and not plagiarism, I just look to them for cool ideas for &quot;what if&quot; scenarios that can spawn original chronicle ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with Charlaquin. Not to discount the presence of colonialist thought and antisemitism in certain real life fringe theories, but it's called the World of Darkness for a reason. <b>The God-Machine Chronicle </b>is practically built on fringe conspiracy tropes.<br /> <br /> Using conspiracy theories as an inspiration for a fantasy game isn't the same as endorsing them, as long as one recognises that they're not real, and that there may be a darker side to the reason some people <i>do </i>believe in them (e.g., antisemitism). It would be...I don't mean to be so blunt, but it would be ridiculous to discount a key inspiration of the gameline, at least as far as calling out people for using those inspirations. I mean, your mileage may vary, but it's not lazy in the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:16:40-07:00","id":174554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174479#post174479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pardon my rudeness but conspiracy theories aren't really the best sources especially how impractical they actually are because well even though there are small scale conspiracies however (like Watergate, Iran Contra, etc) but larger the conspiracy is the more implausible it becomes.<br /> <br /> Especially taking anything fringe as sources undermines the original context that they're taken off from which is why I despise any medium that uses &quot;Ancient Astronauts&quot; or &quot;Lost (often more than likely White) Civilizations&quot; like Assassin's Creed and such because they are insult to any educated person's intelligence not to mention the Colonialist roots that it stems from, just like modern conspiracy theories are stemmed from antisemitism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, if I was in the supernatural community and there was a chance my activities were going to surface at all,I'd find masking them as absurd conspiracy theories would be one of the sanest things I could do.<br /> <br /> So thanks for confirming the sanity of that plan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:35:22-07:00","id":174629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174504#post174504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm with Charlaquin. Not to discount the presence of colonialist thought and antisemitism in certain real life fringe theories, but it's called the World of Darkness for a reason. <b>The God-Machine Chronicle </b>is practically built on fringe conspiracy tropes.<br /> <br /> Using conspiracy theories as an inspiration for a fantasy game isn't the same as endorsing them, as long as one recognises that they're not real, and that there may be a darker side to the reason some people <i>do </i>believe in them (e.g., antisemitism). It would be...I don't mean to be so blunt, but it would be ridiculous to discount a key inspiration of the gameline, at least as far as calling out people for using those inspirations. I mean, your mileage may vary, but it's not lazy in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much to add to this since I completely agree. Conspiracy theories are indeed a good source of inspiration for the World of Darkness setting. I used the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacte_de_Famine\" target=\"_blank\">Pacte de Famine</a> one in a Werewolf game and I have a list of others that can inspire interesting plot hooks. I'm especially fond of those born since the Fifties, since they're a true gold mine of inspiration for the God-Machine and Demon.<br /> <br /> As long as you recognize them for what they are, don't endorse them for real and don't cross the line if they veer into sensitive territory for those at the table, I think they're a nice resource to look at when you need ideas to mess with your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-19-2014, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:50:46-07:00","id":174661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174504#post174504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm with Charlaquin. Not to discount the presence of colonialist thought and antisemitism in certain real life fringe theories, but it's called the World of Darkness for a reason. <b>The God-Machine Chronicle </b>is practically built on fringe conspiracy tropes.<br /> <br /> Using conspiracy theories as an inspiration for a fantasy game isn't the same as endorsing them, as long as one recognises that they're not real, and that there may be a darker side to the reason some people <i>do </i>believe in them (e.g., antisemitism). It would be...I don't mean to be so blunt, but it would be ridiculous to discount a key inspiration of the gameline, at least as far as calling out people for using those inspirations. I mean, your mileage may vary, but it's not lazy in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, you're still using them regardless you're endorsing them or not since it's still a major influence in our society and culture and plus you never know that the people who wrote the games might be endorsed by them if not influenced by them (same thing what you're doing now with using conspiracies as a inspiration) because after all anything they write is a microcosm of themselves. Let's not forget that Mark Rein Hagan's father was a Baptist minister which everything he wrote in VTM was based on what he was influenced in his life (hence the origin of the Caine myth and such) hence it's Christian basis as it's byproduct.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, not only is the God-Machine Chronicle based on fringe theories, it's also loosely based on Christianity as well especially Demon: The Descent is even though &quot;Demons&quot; if you used it organically and academic terms, simply means malicious spirit which doesn't have to tie into a fixed origin like all the gamelines in the WoD do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174554#post174554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, if I was in the supernatural community and there was a chance my activities were going to surface at all,I'd find masking them as absurd conspiracy theories would be one of the sanest things I could do.<br /> <br /> So thanks for confirming the sanity of that plan!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well here's the thing, the major problem with settings like WoD where straight off the bat fails epistemology 101 because if you think about, the entire setting is about Supernaturals hiding in plane sight all along where it becomes highly implausible which the point is, They're far loo large to keep it a secret for so long that could have been discovered a long time ago or even worth keeping a secret in the first place. Same thing with large scale conspiracies as well because you build similar theories and come up with reasonings like they're somehow very good covering their tracks which in the end doesn't sound reasonable at all.<br /> <br /> Logically, if supernaturals really existed at any shape or form, then they should be common knowledge by now similar to True Blood, X-Men, and of course any East Asian supernatural movie or tv show especially on Vampires since after all it's a fictional alternative universe world where you can do anything you want with it that doesn't have to resemble 100% like the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-19-2014, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:05:46-07:00","id":174675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174661#post174661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well here's the thing, the major problem with settings like WoD where straight off the bat fails epistemology 101 because if you think about, the entire setting is about Supernaturals hiding in plane sight all along where it becomes highly implausible which the point is, They're far loo large to keep it a secret for so long that could have been discovered a long time ago or even worth keeping a secret in the first place. Same thing with large scale conspiracies as well because you build similar theories and come up with reasonings like they're somehow very good covering their tracks which in the end doesn't sound reasonable at all.<br /> <br /> Logically, if supernaturals really existed at any shape or form, then they should be common knowledge by now similar to True Blood, X-Men, and of course any East Asian supernatural movie or tv show especially on Vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Logically, it would be impossible for so many supernatrual creatures to exist without their presence being known in the real world. However, that shouldn't matter in the game world, because as you said yourself,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174661#post174661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a fictional alternative universe world where you can do anything you want with it that doesn't have to resemble 100% like the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really matter that it's illogical for them to exist hidden in plain sight, because it's fiction and it doesn't have to make logical sense.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't also interesting to present a World of Darkness where the existence of supernatural creatures is widely known about. The &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; shard from Mirrors is all about that, and it's a cool alternate setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:55:05-07:00","id":174697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174675#post174675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. Logically, it would be impossible for so many supernatrual creatures to exist without their presence being known in the real world. However, that shouldn't matter in the game world, because as you said yourself,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter that it's illogical for them to exist hidden in plain sight, because it's fiction and it doesn't have to make logical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thing is, even in the game world there needs to be plausibility on how it's going to work as well. Of course not only that, contexts also do need to be respected as well which is what conspiracy theories and fringe theories <i>don't</i> do...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174675#post174675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that it isn't also interesting to present a World of Darkness where the existence of supernatural creatures is widely known about. The &quot;World of Darkness Revealed&quot; shard from Mirrors is all about that, and it's a cool alternate setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool I'll check it out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T19:07:58-07:00","id":174823,"title":"","content":"I think, as far as the New World of Darkness is concerned, there's a few important things to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> 1. That people don't WANT to know the monsters are out there.<br /> <br /> 2. That the monsters enforce Masquerades which don't rely on actually somehow being invisible and unknown. They instead rely on misinformation, stigmatization and a lack of solid proof. Stigmatization dovetails with #1.<br /> <br /> 3. That they're actually not a secret to the groups that would plausibly uncover them. Taskforce Valkyrie knows of and deals with the existence of ENEs. Cheiron harvests their bodyparts. The Union keeps them out of our backyards. VASCU investigates magical serial killers. Network Zero puts videos on websites of monsters. TFV covers them up. Etc. There's all sorts of organizations who, while simultaneously trying to eliminate supernaturals, want to keep them a secret from people.<br /> <br /> It honestly strikes me that, provided one utilizes those organizations, the secret of the world of darkness isn't that monsters exist, it's that they're not officially acknowledged or accredited. Your average joe doesn't want to know the truth. So the exceptional people that seek it out get swept up in it. All of that comes together pretty nicely, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:10:53-07:00","id":174874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174697#post174697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well thing is, even in the game world there needs to be plausibility on how it's going to work as well. Of course not only that, contexts also do need to be respected as well which is what conspiracy theories and fringe theories <i>don't</i> do...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having difficulty understanding where you draw the line for willing suspension of disbelief. So vampires, spirits, werewolves, actual magic, alchemically reanimated Frankenstein corpses, faeries and the people they kidnap, ghosts, human-ghost hybrids, resurrected mummies, and a nigh-omniscient world encompassing machine that manipulates the lives of every living thing on earth through layers of complex infrastructure and exploiting loopholes in the laws of reality are all within the acceptable limits, but a government cover-up of a crashed alien spacecraft is going too far? I just don't follow the logic. Maybe it would help if I understood what you meant by &quot;context&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:42:22-07:00","id":175379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=174874#post174874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having difficulty understanding where you draw the line for willing suspension of disbelief. So vampires, spirits, werewolves, actual magic, alchemically reanimated Frankenstein corpses, faeries and the people they kidnap, ghosts, human-ghost hybrids, resurrected mummies, and a nigh-omniscient world encompassing machine that manipulates the lives of every living thing on earth through layers of complex infrastructure and exploiting loopholes in the laws of reality are all within the acceptable limits, but a government cover-up of a crashed alien spacecraft is going too far? I just don't follow the logic. Maybe it would help if I understood what you meant by &quot;context&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean by when it comes to 'government coverups of a alien spacecraft' is taking reality of context because most of the 'classified information' involving UFOs (remember it means &quot;Unidentified Flying Object&quot; not a alien space craft which is a modern invented term) is that they cannot explain what it is so they drop the case much like a unsolved murder or involves crashed weather balloons or experimental aircraft (like U2 spy planes) that is part of a non-disclosure agreement (which companies do all the time) as well and also majority of the crashed &quot;alien spacecrafts&quot; are proven to be hoaxes as well.<br /> <br /> Of course where the line is drawn, Supernaturals and Aliens are two separate things which Supernaturals come from religious cosmologies while Aliens are basically theosophy versions of supernaturals (which traces back to the medieval belief of Angels residing in the 9 planets which theosophy turned that into 'space aliens') which the main point is, you could just might as well use the original mystical ones. Of course however as for actual extraterrestrial life, if you apply the Rare Earth Hypothesis, it's highly likely we're a extremely rare case in the universe because things have to be set very right so it means it's extremely unlikely that Space Aliens are flying around or building galactic empires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-20-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T11:25:29-07:00","id":175422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=175379#post175379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I mean by when it comes to 'government coverups of a alien spacecraft' is taking reality of context because most of the 'classified information' involving UFOs (remember it means &amp;quot;Unidentified Flying Object&amp;quot; not a alien space craft which is a modern invented term) is that they cannot explain what it is so they drop the case much like a unsolved murder or involves crashed weather balloons or experimental aircraft (like U2 spy planes) that is part of a non-disclosure agreement (which companies do all the time) as well and also majority of the crashed &amp;quot;alien spacecrafts&amp;quot; are proven to be hoaxes as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I understand that conspiracy theories are all convincingly presented bullshit that take things out of context to make them seem plausible when they're not. What I don't understand is why you are so offended by the idea of a completely fictional setting that uses some ideas from these theories, with full understanding that they're not true in real life. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course where the line is drawn, Supernaturals and Aliens are two separate things which Supernaturals come from religious cosmologies while Aliens are basically theosophy versions of supernaturals (which traces back to the medieval belief of Angels residing in the 9 planets which theosophy turned that into 'space aliens') which the main point is, you could just might as well use the original mystical ones. Of course however as for actual extraterrestrial life, if you apply the Rare Earth Hypothesis, it's highly likely we're a extremely rare case in the universe because things have to be set very right so it means it's extremely unlikely that Space Aliens are flying around or building galactic empires. </div> </div> </div> Less likely than extradimensional life (Fae and spirits)? Less likely than reanimation of dead tissue (vampires, mummies, and Prometheans)? Less likely than a machine that was created before the evolution of intelligent life on earth but coincidentally happens to use technology that strongly resembles our own, but is sentient, self-aware, and able to bend the laws of physics (the God-Machine)? Even if you follow rare earth hypothesis (which, by the way, is not a very widely accepted theory), we do have actual evidence that intelligent life is possible and naturally occurring, which means as unlikely as it may or may not be, it is possible for it to have evolved elsewhere in the universe. On the other hand, we have no evidence whatsoever for the other things in the World of Darkness that you seem to have no problem accepting within the fiction. There's nothing wrong with liking supernatural fiction and not liking scifi, but to try to call the latter less realistic just doesn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T12:54:14-07:00","id":175493,"title":"","content":"With a lot of conspiracy theories and suspension of disbelief issues it's a lot easier to drop something in that could be there that you lack proof of than to change around something you do have proof of existing in a certain way.<br /> <br /> The way Pentex tends to be presented as destroying the environment to kill off the weres because they're evil, infested with wyrm forces and incidentally are the most profitable and major corporation in the world is an example of this. It's backwards and thus hard to swallow. On the surface all the boxes are checked: Big companies are rich? Check. Big companies pollute? Check. Big companies are often noted for being soulless and having no cares about the individuals or people they impact? Check.<br /> <br /> The problem is that as soon as you work with such entities you quickly realize that the pollution is a side effect, treating people poorly is a side effect. It's all focused on making as much money in a given time frame as possible, and the rest of it is a result of that. And that said companies are insanely cutthroat with each other, if one fails to take an opportunity or makes a misstep someone else will profit from it.<br /> <br /> Thus that presentation of Pentex is bad, because it builds it in a manner contrary to what I know happens. It's not &quot;money is a side issue&quot;, any major corp that isn't scrambling for money is going to get eaten by the ones that are. Oil companies are not Saturday morning cartoon villains poisoning the lake for the lulls, it's done because it's the most profitable way to do what they need to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> So werewolves, vampires, or mages secretly living among us and influencing decisions? A *lot* easier to swallow since I don't have evidence against it. A Company that's the most profitable while having profit as a secondary goal? That's harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:16:12-07:00","id":175502,"title":"","content":"I assume that's CWoD stuff, which I don't know anything about, but it just sounds like a poorly portrayed antagonist. That's not really what we're talking about here though. If we're already accepting that vampires are real and Vlad the Impaler was one (because both are default assumptions of both Worlds of Darkness), how is it too much of a stretch or in any way lazy to say that he had a secret daughter (or more likely a secret childe, since he's a vampire) who absconded with his torpid body and buried it in a tomb in Italy, and use that as a plot point in the game? If we're already accepting that there is a piece of Sufficiently Advanced supertechnology that has been manipulating our lives and the lives of our ancestors from the moment they congealed out of the primordial soup (a default assumption of the God-Machine Chronicle), how is it too much of a stretch or in any way lazy to say that it was built by Sufficiently Advanced life forms from elsewhere in the universe? Personally, I find that an awful lot more plausible than this literal machine with godlike powers just developing organically on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T19:08:29-07:00","id":184318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=175422#post175422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I understand that conspiracy theories are all convincingly presented bullshit that take things out of context to make them seem plausible when they're not. What I don't understand is why you are so offended by the idea of a completely fictional setting that uses some ideas from these theories, with full understanding that they're not true in real life. Less likely than extradimensional life (Fae and spirits)? Less likely than reanimation of dead tissue (vampires, mummies, and Prometheans)? Less likely than a machine that was created before the evolution of intelligent life on earth but coincidentally happens to use technology that strongly resembles our own, but is sentient, self-aware, and able to bend the laws of physics (the God-Machine)? Even if you follow rare earth hypothesis (which, by the way, is not a very widely accepted theory), we do have actual evidence that intelligent life is possible and naturally occurring, which means as unlikely as it may or may not be, it is possible for it to have evolved elsewhere in the universe. On the other hand, we have no evidence whatsoever for the other things in the World of Darkness that you seem to have no problem accepting within the fiction. There's nothing wrong with liking supernatural fiction and not liking scifi, but to try to call the latter less realistic just doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all, while this may sound strange at first but supernatural and 'extra-dimensional' beings are more 'plausible' because they are magical beings which they can do anything which makes anything possible but Extra-Terrestrials however though since they come from another planet, they are bound by material laws and they are not supernatural beings at all but theoretically like us so it's really implausible for them to travel in space at long distances or building colonies in other planets due to hostility of space itself, and other things (from their own home planet since if they returned light years from there, it might be the distant future than they left it). Otherwise like I said, if you apply the rare earth hypothesis, we're likely a very rare occurrence after all.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we often treat Extra-Terrestrials as 'godlike' which is a another example of Theosophy which is simply wrapping supernaturals around secular language while they mean the same thing which you might as well use the supernatural ones because they are really interchangeable but still mean the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=175502#post175502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that's CWoD stuff, which I don't know anything about, but it just sounds like a poorly portrayed antagonist. That's not really what we're talking about here though. If we're already accepting that vampires are real and Vlad the Impaler was one (because both are default assumptions of both Worlds of Darkness), how is it too much of a stretch or in any way lazy to say that he had a secret daughter (or more likely a secret childe, since he's a vampire) who absconded with his torpid body and buried it in a tomb in Italy, and use that as a plot point in the game? If we're already accepting that there is a piece of Sufficiently Advanced supertechnology that has been manipulating our lives and the lives of our ancestors from the moment they congealed out of the primordial soup (a default assumption of the God-Machine Chronicle), how is it too much of a stretch or in any way lazy to say that it was built by Sufficiently Advanced life forms from elsewhere in the universe? Personally, I find that an awful lot more plausible than this literal machine with godlike powers just developing organically on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a Italian Noble was buried there not Vlad Tepes or anyone related to him which is where the context comes in.<br /> <br /> BTW...I forgot to point out that the &quot;God Machine&quot; sounds awefully alike the Christian God turned into a machine to me especially how it's described here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=175493#post175493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So werewolves, vampires, or mages secretly living among us and influencing decisions? A *lot* easier to swallow since I don't have evidence against it. A Company that's the most profitable while having profit as a secondary goal? That's harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well another beef I have with this is that, the very concept of conspiracy and &quot;Forces secretly living among us and influencing decisions&quot; is entirely a christian concept or rather has anti-Semitic origins to it.<br /> <br /> What I would have liked better is if it's &quot;Humanity leads and supernaturals follow&quot; or &quot;We know supernatural existence already&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-29-2014, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T19:34:22-07:00","id":184326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184318#post184318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Italian Noble was buried there not Vlad Tepes or anyone related to him which is where the context comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand that that is the case in real life. What I'm asking is, what is so wrong with taking not even the specific case, but the underlying idea that Vlad the impaler may have had a secret childe who is hiding his torpid body, in a work of fiction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184318#post184318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW...I forgot to point out that the &quot;God Machine&quot; sounds awefully alike the Christian God turned into a machine to me especially how it's described here which speaking of which, If you interchanged Sufficiently Advanced life forms and Supernatural beings, it'll be the same thing which you might as well use the supernatural ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is exactly what it is supposed to sound like, because that's how it's presented in the books. And of course it's interchangeable with supernatural rather than technological power, that's the entire concept behind Clarke's third law. All you're managing to say here is that you like supernatural fiction and you don't like science fiction. Which is fine, but that's your personal preference, not some objective quality that makes science fiction inherently worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T19:51:00-07:00","id":184339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184326#post184326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I understand that that is the case in real life. What I'm asking is, what is so wrong with taking not even the specific case, but the underlying idea that Vlad the impaler may have had a secret childe who is hiding his torpid body, in a work of fiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because even fiction needs to be accurate to real life as well, if you want a secret childe you might as well have a torpid body in a fictional place that doesn't exist in our world. Point is, real life and fiction need to know their bounds to set them apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184326#post184326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that is exactly what it is supposed to sound like, because that's how it's presented in the books. And of course it's interchangeable with supernatural rather than technological power, that's the entire concept behind Clarke's third law. All you're managing to say here is that you like supernatural fiction and you don't like science fiction. Which is fine, but that's your personal preference, not some objective quality that makes science fiction inherently worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the God Machine IS in the end the Christian God despite I heard before I heard 'otherwise' here. You know I'm about to point out how problematic this really is because it's simply using Christianity as a basis while it apparently illegitimatizes other religions just like both Demon games did which at the other hand, instead of using &quot;Demon&quot; academically and generically, they have to attach a Christian context by default which is the real problem here I have with WoD games in general.<br /> <br /> Also as for Supernatural Fiction and Science Fiction, I think it's quite noticeable that I like the former and both genres need to know their boundaries unless they are done right without one invading the other which for example Technobabbling &quot;God is a Machine&quot; &quot;Supernatural beings are Aliens&quot; &quot;Magic is Advanced Technology&quot; and so on which is a proper of example of what Theosophy is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 06-29-2014, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T20:22:44-07:00","id":184351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184339#post184339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because even fiction needs to be accurate to real life as well, if you want a secret childe you might as well have a torpid body in a fictional place that doesn't exist in our world. Point is, real life and fiction need to know their bounds to set them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>But once again, if fiction needs to be accurate to real life, there shouldn't be vampires in the first place. And saying Vlad the impaler became a vampire ignores the &quot;context&quot; that he died in real life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184339#post184339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the God Machine IS in the end the Christian God despite I heard before I heard 'otherwise' here. You know I'm about to point out how problematic this really is because it's simply using Christianity as a basis while it apparently illegitimatizes other religions just like both Demon games did which at the other hand, instead of using &quot;Demon&quot; academically and generically, they have to attach a Christian context by default which is the real problem here I have with WoD games in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the ambiguity there, I was agreeing with your statement that that it is <i>like</i> the Judeo-Christian god. You didn't say it is <i>literally</i> the Judeo-Christian God. It's not. It's actually much more akin to the Gnostic Demiurge than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/172759-the-tomb-of-vlad-dracula-may-have-been-found-in-italy?p=184339#post184339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as for Supernatural Fiction and Science Fiction, I think it's quite noticeable that I like the former and both genres need to know their boundaries unless they are done right without one invading the other which for example Technobabbling &quot;God is a Machine&quot; &quot;Supernatural beings are Aliens&quot; &quot;Magic is Advanced Technology&quot; and so on which is a proper of example of what Theosophy is.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you have a problem with the concept of technology that is beyond our capability to understand, is that correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}